{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Two names stood before the pray[Dm]ing room
[Eb]Joseph called Justus [Bb]sought the light [F]
[Bb]A witness to the [Dm]risen Lord
[Eb]From John's baptism to the fi[F]nal flight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Show us [F/A]which of these you [Gm7]chose
[Eb]Lord you know the [Bb]human [F]heart
[Bb]The lot [F/A]fell not on Jus[Gm7]tus
But the [Eb]witness [F]role was [Bb]marked
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In the upper room they gathered one [Dm]hundred and twenty
[Eb]Praying with the women and the [Bb]mother Mary [F]
[Bb]He walked with Jesus all [Dm]the days
[Eb]An eyewitness to the [F]victory
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
